        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rajendralal Mitra, the Coptic-born philologist and Orientalist, the person who coined transtheism\n- Roles: philologists, Orientalists, Coptic scholars, Indologists\n- Concepts: transtheism, Indian philology\n\nFacts:\n- The Coptic-born philologist and Orientalist lived in Britain for most of his life.\n- The Coptic-born philologist and Orientalist is considered one of the most important Coptic scholars in Indian philology.\n- The person who coined the term transtheism worked on Indology.\n- Rajendralal Mitra had the same profession as the person who coined transtheism, namely philologist.",
