        "original_id": "1e858803-d005-5e39-95e9-a41053e7433f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Heinrich Zimmer, Max Müller, Paul Tillich, Rajendralal Mitra\n- Roles: German scholar, philologist, Orientalist, Indologist, philosopher\n- Concepts: Indian Philology, Indology, transtheism, Bengal Renaissance\n\nFacts:\n- Max Müller was born on 6 December 1823 and died on 28 October 1900.\n- Max Müller was a German-born philologist and Orientalist who lived and studied in Britain for most of his life.\n- Max Müller wrote both scholarly and popular works on Indology.\n- Rajendralal Mitra was born on 15 February 1824 and died on 26 July 1891.\n- Rajendralal Mitra was the first modern Indologist of Indian origin and a key figure in the Bengal Renaissance.\n- Heinrich Zimmer was considered the most important German scholar in Indian Philology after Max Müller.\n- Transtheism is a term coined by either Paul Tillich or Heinrich Zimmer for a religious or philosophical system that is neither theistic nor atheistic, but beyond both.",
